# Google Analytics (playrival.app)

Every **public-facing HTML page** on playrival.app must include Google Analytics with **Consent Mode v2** and the shared cookie-consent script. Measurement ID: `G-R445NE2NSX`.

## Required on each page

1. **Google tag in `<head>`** — first content inside `<head>`, before `<meta charset>`. Do not add more than one Google tag per page.

```html
<!-- Google tag (gtag.js) — Consent Mode v2 -->
<script async src="https://www.googletagmanager.com/gtag/js?id=G-R445NE2NSX"></script>
<script>
  window.dataLayer = window.dataLayer || [];
  function gtag(){dataLayer.push(arguments);}
  gtag("consent", "default", {
    analytics_storage: "denied",
    ad_storage: "denied",
    ad_user_data: "denied",
    ad_personalization: "denied",
    wait_for_update: 500,
  });
  gtag("js", new Date());
  gtag("config", "G-R445NE2NSX");
</script>
```

2. **Cookie consent script before `</body>`** — use the same cache version as other local JS (see cache-busting rule):

- Root pages (`index.html`, `privacy.html`, `terms.html`): `js/analytics.js?v=<N>`
- Nested pages (`download/`, `support/`, etc.): `../js/analytics.js?v=<N>`

```html
<script defer src="js/analytics.js?v=36"></script>
```

## When adding or editing pages

- **New HTML page** → add both snippets above; link `css/main.css` with the current `?v=` (nested pages use `../css/`).
- **Copy from an existing page** in the same folder depth so paths stay correct.
- **Do not** load GA on non-site files (e.g. templates, drafts) if they are not deployed pages.
- **Privacy policy** — if analytics behavior or cookies change, update `privacy.html` (section `#cookies`) and bump its effective date.

## Do not

- Remove Consent Mode defaults or load analytics without `js/analytics.js`.
- Put the measurement ID in a secret env file — it is public by design; keep logic in `js/analytics.js`, not duplicated inline beyond the gtag block.
